<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.alphalete.org-board-slack</string>

    <!-- Path is the laptop placeholder; on the mini, install_agent.py rewrites it
         to the mini's repo path (python -m automations.day_orchestrator.install_agent
         org-board-slack). -->
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder/deploy/org_board_slack.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PYTHONPATH</key>
        <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder</string>
    </dict>

    <!-- DAILY incl. weekends (no Weekday key). First pass 7:05 CST (Eve
         2026-08-12; it was 8:30 when Megan wired this on 2026-07-18 to match the
         VA's ~8:05-8:17 post, then 07:15 on 08-11), then q25m retries as a
         safety net.
         The module's LIGHT gate posts unless yesterday is entirely empty, and a
         once-per-day state file no-ops the remaining passes. TIME KNOB: edit
         these entries (Hour/Minute are machine LOCAL time; the mini is Central). -->
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <array>
        <!-- EARLY SLOTS PREPENDED, first one 07:05 (Eve 2026-08-12); the
             original 08:30..11:25 grid below is untouched.

             WHY 07:05. This slot chases the FILL, and the fill's clock changed
             on 2026-08-12: org_sales_board no longer waits for the BOX extract
             (the 'tableau:box_daily' gate was removed — see that report's
             _box_gate_note in schedule_config.json) and now runs behind a
             not_before '06:35' floor instead. The fill takes 9-14 min, so it
             ENDS ~06:44-06:49 rather than the 07:04-07:11 that justified the
             07:15 slot this replaces. 07:05 clears that tail with margin and
             puts the REVIEW LINK — which lands ~4 min after this post, because
             org_sales_board_email is gated on slack:org_board_posted — at about
             07:10-07:15, which is what Eve asked for.

             07:05 -> 06:55 (Eve 2026-08-13). The fill no longer waits for the
             orchestrator's serial pass at all — org_sales_board moved to order
             4.95 and ends ~05:20 — so the tail this slot was chasing is gone,
             and the ask moved with it: the REVIEW LINK has to be up at 07:00
             (com.alphalete.org-board-review-post), which means the public post
             has to be already out. 06:55 puts it there; the q25m ladder below
             is unchanged and still covers a late board.

             06:55 -> 07:05 (Eve 2026-08-25), TO GET BOX INTO THIS PICTURE.
             Until now this post showed a BOX section a day behind — the
             accepted trade from 2026-08-12 ('aunque Box esté siempre un día
             atrasado'), because the Box extract does not land until
             ~06:50-08:00 and the fill runs at 04:50. The trade was only ever
             needed for the FULL fill (5 sections + captainships, 9-14 min);
             ONE section is 2-5 min, so com.alphalete.org-board-box-repull now
             tops off Box alone at 06:52 / 06:58 and this post moved behind it.
             Ten minutes buys a current Box on most mornings.

             THIS SLOT MUST STAY AFTER THE BOX RE-PULL. Exporting the PNG while
             that pull is mid-write screenshots a half-written BOX block, which
             is worse than a day-behind one; org_board_slack.sh hard-waits for
             the re-pull process before it exports, but the clock should not be
             relying on that guard. Move this and move 06:52/06:58 with it.

             ON A MORNING BOX IS STILL LATE the re-pull no-ops and this post
             goes out at 07:05 with Box a day behind — exactly the old
             behaviour, never a delay. The 2:30pm board-catchup still fixes the
             board itself either way. slack_post.fill_gate is LIGHT — it holds
             only if yesterday is empty across EVERY section — so a blank BOX
             column does not push this to the next slot. -->
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>7</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>5</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>7</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>7</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>55</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>8</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>8</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>55</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>9</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>20</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>9</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>45</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>10</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>10</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>10</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>35</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>11</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>11</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>25</integer></dict>
    </array>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder/output/logs/org-board-slack.launchd.out.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/megan/1st Claude Folder/output/logs/org-board-slack.launchd.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
